A||N||6||FieroJoe||Trunk rust in really wierd place...||||13||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||03-24-2001||11:30 PM||||Well, I finally found rust in my never-winter driven Fiero.  It is in the trunk, but not in the usual spot.  I thougth that the trunks most likely rusted out at the bottom, but my bottom is about as solid as it was the day it was welded together.  My trunk has rusted through on the sides, (see pics), and also a part of the frame rail that is near there had some pinholes in it.  So I spent today grinding and cutting and welding it all up, and then using seam sealer (white crap) and spray undercoating.<P>Anybody else have their cars rust out there?<P>new sheet metal welded in:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010046.jpg"> <P>left side, inside finish with seam sealer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010053.jpg"> <P>right side, rust through hole cleaned up, ready for welding:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010045.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Songman||03-24-2001||11:46 PM||||That is the usual place I have seen rust. I've never seen on rust out in the bottom. But of course, I haven't inspected a lot of trunks anyway! hehe<P>Looks like you did a nice job on the repair.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||03-25-2001||10:21 AM||||If your trunk is rusted there you might also check your shock tower on the outside top surface.  It is where much of the road grime is getting in. I don't know if you will be able to visually see it.  It is the top of the same frame rail that rusted in the trunk of your car. I found rust there when I had the cradle and struts out on one of ours. The road grime gets in there and runs down to the trunk and starts all the grief.  I now clean and reseal the stut towers anytime the struts are out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||03-25-2001||10:41 AM||||I have never seen rust on the bottom, only the sides<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||mope||03-25-2001||09:54 PM||||HEY!!! that looks better than my trunk did! I cut and fixed mine too. mine looks like new...sorta<P>m0pe<P>------------------<BR>=======================<P>-= Silver 86 GT, being restored, and following major things to be done: Mr. Mike's Leather, new steering wheel, paint repair, ebrake repair, take apart and clean everything! <A HREF="http://www.mastergraphics.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mope.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mope.cjb.net</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||mope||03-25-2001||09:55 PM||||oh yeah, check your other side too, i guarentee you it will be worse over there. its hard to see from in the trunk, so you hafta take out all the wheel well plastic.<P>have fun, i did!!!<P>m0pe||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||03-25-2001||10:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>oh yeah, check your other side too, i guarentee you it will be worse over there. its hard to see from in the trunk, so you hafta take out all the wheel well plastic.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah I fixed the stuff on the rails too, I had to take out the plastic to weld from the other side and to spray undercoating.<P>Those little push fasteners with the phillips screw in the middle of them that hold on the wheel well plastic are a PITA to get off!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
